00:31:55,200 --> 00:31:56,440
Who is your dad?

568
00:31:57,119 --> 00:31:59,400
Tell me! Who is your dad?

569
00:32:01,160 --> 00:32:02,559
What happened in the bamboo forest that day...

570
00:32:02,559 --> 00:32:03,519
wasn't Dad's fault.

571
00:32:03,640 --> 00:32:04,880
Who is your dad?

572
00:32:05,000 --> 00:32:06,079
Wang Zhiping.

573
00:32:06,079 --> 00:32:06,839
Mom told you.

574
00:32:07,039 --> 00:32:08,599
Who is your dad?

575
00:32:10,559 --> 00:32:11,359
No...

576
00:32:13,359 --> 00:32:14,000
I...

577
00:32:15,240 --> 00:32:16,519
I don't have a dad.

578
00:32:45,720 --> 00:32:47,359
Mom, from now on, every day I'll

579
00:32:47,359 --> 00:32:48,839
voluntarily hand in my work diary,

580
00:32:49,200 --> 00:32:50,400
so you won't have to search my room.

581
00:32:55,359 --> 00:32:57,480
So you're blaming me for going through your things?

582
00:32:57,680 --> 00:33:00,000
Mom, I know you care about me.

583
00:33:00,319 --> 00:33:02,359
I'm just trying to accommodate your concern.

584
00:33:02,480 --> 00:33:03,039
I didn't mean to...

585
00:33:03,039 --> 00:33:03,799
Let me ask you this.

586
00:33:04,039 --> 00:33:05,079
First thing the day before yesterday,

587
00:33:05,119 --> 00:33:07,000
didn't I tell you we were taking a family portrait?

588
00:33:08,160 --> 00:33:09,920
And told you to get off work early?

589
00:33:11,000 --> 00:33:11,839
Where were you?

590
00:33:15,359 --> 00:33:16,839
Do you know how many times I called?

591
00:33:17,240 --> 00:33:18,400
How many messages I sent?

592
00:33:18,400 --> 00:33:19,440
Did you reply to any of them?

593
00:33:20,720 --> 00:33:21,720
It's early in the morning.

594
00:33:21,720 --> 00:33:22,960
The kid didn't say anything bad.

595
00:33:22,960 --> 00:33:24,279
What's with that attitude?

596
00:33:28,200 --> 00:33:29,160
You have no heart,

597
00:33:29,400 --> 00:33:30,799
and no conscience either, is that it?

598
00:33:31,000 --> 00:33:31,839
Look at Director Fan

599
00:33:31,839 --> 00:33:33,240
and the other kids.

600
00:33:33,559 --> 00:33:35,279
Whose life is always smooth sailing?

601
00:33:35,599 --> 00:33:36,920
How come every single one of them

602
00:33:36,920 --> 00:33:37,680
has stepped out of the shadows?

603
00:33:37,680 --> 00:33:38,799
Why is it just you

604
00:33:38,799 --> 00:33:40,160
always walking around with a long face?

605
00:33:42,119 --> 00:33:43,599
I know you guys are doing this for my own good.

606
00:33:43,599 --> 00:33:45,359
You want me to let go of the past and move on.

607
00:33:46,160 --> 00:33:47,640
But I make my own choices.

608
00:33:49,160 --> 00:33:49,880
Didn't you just ask me

609
00:33:49,880 --> 00:33:51,160
when we took the family portrait the day before yesterday,

610
00:33:51,160 --> 00:33:52,160
where I was?

611
00:33:53,680 --> 00:33:55,720
I just want to say I couldn't go.

612
00:34:00,119 --> 00:34:01,519
And I'm truly, from the bottom of my heart,

613
00:34:01,519 --> 00:34:02,440
happy for you.

614
00:34:03,480 --> 00:34:04,799
You've completely moved on.

615
00:34:05,480 --> 00:34:06,240
What do you mean by that?

616
00:34:06,240 --> 00:34:07,559
Make yourself clear!

617
00:34:11,119 --> 00:34:11,880
The day before yesterday

618
00:34:13,519 --> 00:34:14,639
was my dad's death anniversary.

619
00:34:28,119 --> 00:34:28,880
Wang Ning

620
00:34:29,920 --> 00:34:31,440
Mommy has to work. Be good, okay?

621
00:34:41,280 --> 00:34:42,239
We're about to head out on a mission.

622
00:34:42,880 --> 00:34:44,719
Go back. Your child is still waiting.

623
00:35:07,119 --> 00:35:08,280
Do you have any accomplices?

624
00:35:09,800 --> 00:35:10,920
Can't you save us some trouble?

625
00:35:11,360 --> 00:35:12,400
Of all the things you could do,

626
00:35:12,559 --> 00:35:13,679
you chose to deal drugs.

627
00:35:14,840 --> 00:35:15,840
Playing tough, huh?

628
00:35:16,639 --> 00:35:17,119
Come clean.

629
00:35:17,800 --> 00:35:18,679
Do you have any accomplices?

630
00:35:26,320 --> 00:35:27,159
Ding Kuihai.

631
00:35:29,039 --> 00:35:30,119
This is Uncle Ding.

632
00:35:31,360 --> 00:35:32,360
Go ahead and say hi.

633
00:35:33,480 --> 00:35:35,519
How are you, kiddo?

634
00:35:35,920 --> 00:35:36,639
Say hello to Uncle.

635
00:35:37,639 --> 00:35:39,199
Here, let's shake hands.

636
00:36:10,880 --> 00:36:11,519
Hello.

637
00:36:12,440 --> 00:36:14,400
I'm your current defense attorney, Ding Ning.

638
00:36:15,039 --> 00:36:16,760
I'd like to ask you a few questions first.

639
00:36:17,000 --> 00:36:17,679
Go ahead.

640
00:36:18,360 --> 00:36:20,480
Actually, our nursing home

641
00:36:21,079 --> 00:36:23,039
isn't dealing with this for the first time.

642
00:36:23,760 --> 00:36:25,440
The reason I'm pleading guilty

643
00:36:26,000 --> 00:36:27,000
is because

644
00:36:28,400 --> 00:36:31,039
is because they promised me a sum of money.

645
00:36:31,440 --> 00:36:32,199
After the trial begins,

646
00:36:32,199 --> 00:36:34,239
the nursing home will secretly give you a deposit.

647
00:36:34,239 --> 00:36:35,000
Once the trial ends,

648
00:36:35,000 --> 00:36:36,039
they'll transfer the rest of the money

649
00:36:36,039 --> 00:36:37,280
to your girlfriend's account.

650
00:36:37,280 --> 00:36:38,440
But based on the agreement

651
00:36:38,440 --> 00:36:40,079
Chang Yu had both of you sign,

652
00:36:40,360 --> 00:36:41,559
if you back out halfway

653
00:36:41,559 --> 00:36:43,440
or talk nonsense online after your release,

654
00:36:43,679 --> 00:36:45,599
you'll have to pay the nursing home triple.

655
00:36:45,719 --> 00:36:46,519
Understand?

656
00:36:46,519 --> 00:36:47,400
Understood.

657
00:36:47,880 --> 00:36:48,639
Good.

658
00:36:50,039 --> 00:36:52,360
I won't talk nonsense, and I won't back out.

659
00:36:53,840 --> 00:36:56,159
I saw the kite a few days ago.

660
00:36:58,000 --> 00:36:58,960
How is she?

661
00:36:59,199 --> 00:36:59,880
Not good.

662
00:37:01,559 --> 00:37:02,960
She believes more than you do

663
00:37:02,960 --> 00:37:04,320
that you're innocent.

664
00:37:04,519 --> 00:37:05,599
She'd rather be heavily pregnant

665
00:37:05,599 --> 00:37:07,119
handing out flyers at the mall

666
00:37:07,239 --> 00:37:09,360
than take a single cent from the nursing home.

667
00:37:09,920 --> 00:37:10,800
That's just how she is.

668
00:37:12,320 --> 00:37:14,599
How much is innocence worth anyway?

669
00:37:14,719 --> 00:37:15,480
If having money

670
00:37:15,480 --> 00:37:18,199
means giving my girlfriend and my child

671
00:37:18,440 --> 00:37:19,719
a better life,

672
00:37:20,039 --> 00:37:22,320
that's what matters, right?

673
00:37:23,480 --> 00:37:24,639
Are you asking me?

674
00:37:26,000 --> 00:37:27,400
Or are you trying to convince yourself?

675
00:37:30,639 --> 00:37:32,280
I'm going to start explaining the trial procedure.

676
00:37:32,559 --> 00:37:33,440
Wait, Lawyer Ding.

677
00:37:34,519 --> 00:37:35,639
I have another question.

678
00:37:36,199 --> 00:37:38,559
I just really want to know,

679
00:37:38,800 --> 00:37:42,079
kids whose fathers are criminals,

680
00:37:44,039 --> 00:37:45,960
how do they end up growing up?

681
00:38:01,599 --> 00:38:03,159
I will now go over the court procedures.

682
00:38:59,199 --> 00:39:01,440
Bring in the defendant, Zhang Lin.

683
00:39:10,639 --> 00:39:11,360
Prosecutor.

684
00:39:12,079 --> 00:39:14,159
Isn't the victim testifying today?

685
00:39:14,159 --> 00:39:15,440
Why hasn't she arrived yet?

686
00:39:16,559 --> 00:39:17,360
Ten minutes.

687
00:39:18,440 --> 00:39:19,400
We've already spoken to her.

688
00:39:19,400 --> 00:39:20,360
She's stuck in traffic.

689
00:39:20,360 --> 00:39:21,320
She should be here shortly.

690
00:39:22,559 --> 00:39:23,679
In the interest of time,

691
00:39:24,000 --> 00:39:24,960
let's begin.

692
00:39:25,320 --> 00:39:28,440
Fulin District People's Court of Jiangliu City.

693
00:39:29,039 --> 00:39:30,159
The court is now in session.

694
00:39:31,360 --> 00:39:32,840
The beginning is all routine.

695
00:39:33,079 --> 00:39:34,599
After asking your name and birthdate,

696
00:39:34,599 --> 00:39:35,559
they'll introduce the court staff,

697
00:39:35,559 --> 00:39:36,760
and read your legal rights.

698
00:39:36,840 --> 00:39:38,639
Then we enter the court investigation phase.

699
00:39:38,920 --> 00:39:40,639
The prosecutor will read the indictment.

700
00:39:41,960 --> 00:39:42,800
And then...

701
00:39:44,920 --> 00:39:45,920
here comes the important part.

702
00:39:47,360 --> 00:39:49,639
Go on, I'm listening.

703
00:39:51,599 --> 00:39:52,719
The judge will ask you,

704
00:39:53,480 --> 00:39:55,840
regarding the criminal facts charged in the indictment,

705
00:39:55,840 --> 00:39:57,840
if you have any objections, and what they are.

706
00:39:58,719 --> 00:39:59,639
In other words,

707
00:40:00,920 --> 00:40:01,960
do you plead guilty or not?

708
00:40:02,920 --> 00:40:04,239
The prosecutor, Lei Xiaopeng,

709
00:40:04,800 --> 00:40:05,599
has finished reading.

710
00:40:06,519 --> 00:40:07,239
Defendant,

711
00:40:08,599 --> 00:40:09,599
do you have any objections?

712
00:40:11,280 --> 00:40:11,920
I can guess

713
00:40:11,920 --> 00:40:13,760
what you've heard over the past three months.

714
00:40:14,599 --> 00:40:15,400
For instance,

715
00:40:15,639 --> 00:40:17,800
the national success rate for not-guilty pleas last year

716
00:40:17,800 --> 00:40:19,519
was only 0.0384 percent.

717
00:40:19,639 --> 00:40:20,440
In other words,

718
00:40:20,840 --> 00:40:22,320
out of ten thousand criminal cases,

719
00:40:22,320 --> 00:40:23,880
the successful not-guilty pleas

720
00:40:23,880 --> 00:40:25,039
are fewer than four.

721
00:40:25,920 --> 00:40:27,320
Whether a not-guilty plea will succeed,

722
00:40:27,440 --> 00:40:28,679
no one can be absolutely certain.

723
00:40:28,679 --> 00:40:29,719
There's no point discussing that.

724
00:40:30,159 --> 00:40:31,599
What is truly meaningful and valuable

725
00:40:31,880 --> 00:40:33,760
are the trade-offs behind this case.

726
00:40:34,159 --> 00:40:35,039
If you plead guilty,

727
00:40:35,599 --> 00:40:36,679
we already have a letter of forgiveness.

728
00:40:36,679 --> 00:40:37,760
You might only get one year,

729
00:40:37,880 --> 00:40:38,880
or even probation.

730
00:40:39,480 --> 00:40:40,639
If you insist on pleading not guilty,

731
00:40:41,000 --> 00:40:41,920
and you happen to fail,

732
00:40:42,880 --> 00:40:44,639
nine times out of ten, you'll get five years minimum.

733
00:40:45,440 --> 00:40:46,679
But all of that is nonsense.

734
00:40:48,039 --> 00:40:48,719
You asked me just now,

735
00:40:48,719 --> 00:40:50,800
how a child grows up with a criminal father.

736
00:40:52,400 --> 00:40:53,280
Let me tell you.

737
00:40:54,679 --> 00:40:56,599
Besides being judged by others as a child,

738
00:40:57,480 --> 00:40:58,599
more importantly,

739
00:40:59,159 --> 00:41:00,559
she will instinctively believe

740
00:41:00,559 --> 00:41:02,320
that her father is innocent.

741
00:41:03,400 --> 00:41:04,679
She'll want to, for her father's sake,

742
00:41:04,679 --> 00:41:06,920
or even just for those in a similar situation,

743
00:41:07,320 --> 00:41:08,760
risk her reputation and future

744
00:41:08,760 --> 00:41:10,320
to fight for their innocence.

745
00:41:11,559 --> 00:41:13,159
Even if you accept your fate for money,

746
00:41:14,000 --> 00:41:14,800
she won't.

747
00:41:15,800 --> 00:41:17,719
She'll carry your confusion and regrets,

748
00:41:17,719 --> 00:41:19,239
and go against everyone.

749
00:41:19,440 --> 00:41:20,320
For the rest of her life,

750
00:41:20,320 --> 00:41:21,360
just to fight for

751
00:41:21,360 --> 00:41:22,920
the justice you deserve.

752
00:41:28,559 --> 00:41:29,320
Justice?

753
00:41:30,320 --> 00:41:32,440
What the hell good is justice?

754
00:41:34,440 --> 00:41:36,119
Can the weak really beat the strong?

755
00:41:37,039 --> 00:41:38,400
I just got myself into deep trouble.

756
00:41:38,480 --> 00:41:40,519
I was set up by these people.

757
00:41:42,320 --> 00:41:43,679
What choice do I have?

758
00:41:44,440 --> 00:41:46,039
So why are you giving up?

759
00:41:47,440 --> 00:41:48,800
Why is it that when everyone covers your mouth,

760
00:41:48,840 --> 00:41:50,199
you just obediently shut up?

761
00:41:50,800 --> 00:41:52,199
And then brainwash yourself into believing,

762
00:41:52,199 --> 00:41:53,159
"If I just take this abuse,

763
00:41:53,159 --> 00:41:54,599
things will get better later"?

764
00:41:55,639 --> 00:41:56,920
If you're truly doing this for your partner

765
00:41:56,920 --> 00:41:57,880
and your child,

766
00:41:57,880 --> 00:41:59,760
shouldn't you be crying out your innocence?

767
00:42:00,320 --> 00:42:01,800
How am I supposed to cry out?

768
00:42:01,800 --> 00:42:03,679
"Ah!" Like that? Will that work?

769
00:42:05,519 --> 00:42:06,280
It's perfectly clear that

770
00:42:06,280 --> 00:42:07,639
this is a losing game for me.

771
00:42:09,760 --> 00:42:10,679
To you,

772
00:42:10,679 --> 00:42:12,559
this is just another case.

773
00:42:12,719 --> 00:42:14,440
What price do you pay if you lose?

774
00:42:15,079 --> 00:42:15,880
But what about me?

775
00:42:16,760 --> 00:42:19,960
I'm gambling with the fate of my entire family.

776
00:42:23,000 --> 00:42:23,880
I can't afford to lose.

777
00:42:25,360 --> 00:42:26,559
If my boss, Chang Yu,

778
00:42:26,559 --> 00:42:27,800
finds out I advised you to change your plea,

779
00:42:28,360 --> 00:42:30,039
I'll very likely lose my job.

780
00:42:30,719 --> 00:42:32,119
If I say one thing at the pretrial conference,

781
00:42:32,159 --> 00:42:33,960
and openly change your plea during the trial,

782
00:42:34,559 --> 00:42:35,880
I'll be ostracized

783
00:42:35,880 --> 00:42:37,400
and face endless trouble.

784
00:42:37,960 --> 00:42:39,679
And if this blows up online,

785
00:42:40,199 --> 00:42:41,840
I'll be socially ruined.

786
00:42:43,400 --> 00:42:44,599
Of course, I could be like everyone else

787
00:42:44,599 --> 00:42:45,480
and advise you to give up.

788
00:42:46,599 --> 00:42:47,280
But I'm willing

789
00:42:47,280 --> 00:42:49,039
to use my career as a bargaining chip,

790
00:42:49,039 --> 00:42:50,079
place it in your hands,

791
00:42:50,079 --> 00:42:51,480
and fight alongside you.

792
00:42:52,440 --> 00:42:53,519
What more are you afraid of?

793
00:42:54,679 --> 00:42:55,360
I...

794
00:42:58,280 --> 00:42:59,639
I'm sorry, Lawyer Ding.

795
00:43:00,880 --> 00:43:02,679
I'm sorry, give me a moment.

796
00:43:05,840 --> 00:43:07,639
Even for the most unforgivable criminals,

797
00:43:07,880 --> 00:43:10,079
a defense attorney must stand by their side,

798
00:43:10,079 --> 00:43:12,519
and do everything to protect their legal rights.

799
00:43:12,559 --> 00:43:14,360
This is our duty under the law.

800
00:43:16,280 --> 00:43:17,679
In short, the choice is yours,

801
00:43:18,039 --> 00:43:18,760
not mine.

802
00:43:19,519 --> 00:43:20,840
When you stand in that courtroom,

803
00:43:22,280 --> 00:43:24,079
you might make a more instinctive choice.

804
00:43:25,559 --> 00:43:27,199
I've prepared two defense strategies.

805
00:43:27,360 --> 00:43:29,280
One is what we discussed at the pretrial conference:

806
00:43:29,920 --> 00:43:30,719
we plead guilty and accept the punishment

807
00:43:30,719 --> 00:43:32,079
to seek leniency for you.

808
00:43:33,800 --> 00:43:35,000
The other one...

809
00:43:40,079 --> 00:43:40,719
Defendant,

810
00:43:41,360 --> 00:43:42,360
do you have any objections?

811
00:43:43,880 --> 00:43:46,119
Yes, I have an objection.

812
00:43:48,280 --> 00:43:49,159
What is your objection?

813
00:43:50,119 --> 00:43:50,960
I plead not guilty.

814
00:43:53,440 --> 00:43:54,440
I am innocent.
